<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vidisha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Besnagar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vidisha is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Betwa river near Sanchi. Ancient Vidisha, at nearby Besnagar, was a major trading town of the Maurya and Shunga periods, where the Shunga prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agnimitra">Agnimitra</a> governed and the Greek envoy Heliodorus raised his pillar around 113 BCE. Later it was the centre of a Naga kingdom and of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vidisha.jpg" alt="Vidisha" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suyash Dwivedi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samrat_Ashok_Technological_Institute_main_building.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
